 "_caveats": [
  "Prison figures are a single-day census as on 31 December 2024. They do not count everyone held during the year: a person released in November does not appear.",
  "West Bengal sent NCRB no prison data for 2024, so NCRB reprinted its 2023 figures in every 2024 table, and they are in the national totals here. West Bengal's own bars describe 31 December 2023.",
  "Population and SC/ST shares are Census 2011, the most recent enumerated count India has, since the 2021 census was not held. A rate per 100,000 is therefore 2024 prisoners over people counted in 2011.",
  "'Undertrial' means a person in custody whose trial has not concluded. They have not been convicted of the offence they are held for.",
  "Court pendency counts cases, and one person can be party to several. District and high court figures are from the National Judicial Data Grid as on 9 March 2026, as given to the Lok Sabha on 13 March 2026, which is fourteen months after the prison census.",
  "In that Lok Sabha table Meghalaya's civil and criminal district-court figures (4,917 each) do not add to its printed total of 16,671. The national columns add up only with the printed figures, so the total is used."
 ],
